                <head>No. 209<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>During the last two weeks of March and the first week of April, final
                    arrangements for Jean Monnet’s visit
                    to Washington were made, and a press release was issued on April 1 announcing
                    that these talks would begin on April 6. For the text of this press release, see
                    Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, April 12, 1954, pages
                    562–563. Subsequently, the opening session of the loan negotiations were
                    postponed until April 7 and finally April 8. In preparation for these talks,
                    several briefing memoranda, speaking papers, and background papers were drafted
                    in the Department of State. Copies of these documents, none of which is printed
                    here, are in Conference files, lot 59 D 95, CF 237 and RA files, lot 58 D 374, “Schuman Plan—1954”.</p>
            </div>
